# starters/essays/.cut -- which paths of the full site this starter is cut
# from make up site/.
# One path per line, relative to the full site's root. A directory copies
# recursively. Regenerate from the root of this repository with:
#   scripts/cut-starter.sh <path-to-the-full-site> essays

# moss's own scaffold gitignores, identical between the full site and the
# starter -- not build output, just checked-in convention.
.moss/.gitignore

# site config + gazetteer (places.toml is pruned to referenced places only)
.moss/config.toml
.moss/places.toml

# theme + self-hosted fonts, whole directory
.moss/theme

# portrait (About.md's image)
assets/portrait.jpg

# home name, about (her bibliography now lives as a list item on About.md
# itself, since the full site folded Books.md into it)
Virginia Woolf.md
About.md

# essays: folder index + four essays -- the opening essay, one with
# footnotes (Modern Fiction), and the two essays with `location:` so
# [terms.places] has something to show
Essays/Essays.md
Essays/01-the-common-reader.md
Essays/15-modern-fiction.md
Essays/27-haworth-november-1904.md
Essays/28-to-spain.md

# talks: folder index, one lecture (How Should One Read a Book?, so the
# folder shows more than one kind of occasion), and the Room folder page
# with its first two chapters -- enough for one real prev/next pair
# (chapter 1 -> 2 -> back to 1). The other four Room chapters and Mr
# Bennett and Mrs Brown are cut, see .moss/STARTER.md for why that stays a
# clean two-chapter demo rather than a partial six.
Talks/Talks.md
Talks/00-how-should-one-read-a-book.md
Talks/A Room of One's Own/A Room of One's Own.md
Talks/A Room of One's Own/01-but-you-may-say.md
Talks/A Room of One's Own/02-the-scene-if-i-may-ask-you-to-follow-me.md
